PROBABILITY FUNCTIONS (p_{n}=0)
The direct way to generate Y is to generate \{U\} and put Y=y_{1} if
p_{1}+p_{2}+ . . . +p_{t-1}<U<p_{1}+p_{2}+ . . . +p_{t}.
However, this method requires complicated machine programs that take too long.
An alternative way due to Marsaglia [26.53] is simple, fast, and seems to be well suited to high-speed computations. Let p_{1} for i=1, 2, . . . , n be expressed by k decimal digits as p_{i}=\delta_{ti}a_{kt} . .

